Is this still a bug? Couldn't repro:

```rust
use bevy::ecs::system::SystemParam;
use std::marker::PhantomData;

#[derive(SystemParam)]
pub struct MyParam<'w, 's> {
    foo: Res<'w, FooParamState>,
    #[system_param(ignore)]
    marker: PhantomData<&'s FooParamState>,
}

pub struct FooParamState;
```

That's because you need to specify the `'s` lifetime: https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/2711.

And yup, I can repro now thanks:
```rust
use bevy::ecs::system::SystemParam;
use std::marker::PhantomData;

#[derive(SystemParam)]
pub struct MyParam<'w, 's> {
    foo: Res<'w, MyParamState>,
    #[system_param(ignore)]
    marker: PhantomData<&'s MyParamState>,
}

pub struct MyParamState;
```

