Using just `const _: () = {}` doesn't work because inside that scope there's no way to differentiate between the two identically named structs. I tried various ways of wrapping stuff in a mod, but that didn't work either because of visibility issues. The patch I posted seem to work for everything except a struct declared with the `pub(super)` visibility.
